===Etymology===
{{ety|sw|:inh|bnt-sab-pro:*i̧pika<alt:*-i̧pika>|text=++|tree=1}} From the same root as {{m|sw|epua|-epua|to take off the fire}} (but without retention of the initial {{m|bnt-pro||*-jì-}} syllable) + {{af|sw|-ika<pos:stative>}}.

In Sabaki, cognate with {{cog|zdj|piha|-piha}} and {{cog|coh||-βika}}. Other Bantu cognates include {{cog|zu|pheka|-pheka}} and {{cog|ny|phika|-phika}}.

